        {
          "_type": "block",
          "_key": "dc-what",
          "style": "h3",
          "markDefs": [],
          "children": [
            {
              "_type": "span",
              "_key": "dc-whats1",
              "text": "What are Deacons?",
              "marks": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "_type": "block",
          "_key": "dc-a-1",
          "style": "normal",
          "markDefs": [],
          "children": [
            {
              "_type": "span",
              "_key": "dc-a-1s1",
              "text": "Each active member or attendee is assigned a Deacon whom they can go to with questions, to get connected, or for pastoral care needs.",
              "marks": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "_type": "block",
          "_key": "dc-b-1",
          "style": "normal",
          "markDefs": [],
          "children": [
            {
              "_type": "span",
              "_key": "dc-b-1s1",
              "text": "In the New Testament, deacons were chosen for acts of mercy and service in the church (1 Timothy 3:8-9; Romans 16:1-2).",
              "marks": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "_type": "block",
          "_key": "dc-c-1",
          "style": "normal",
          "markDefs": [],
          "children": [
            {
              "_type": "span",
              "_key": "dc-c-1s1",
              "text": "Following that example, Deacons assist at the Lord’s table and in baptism, in orienting and caring for members, and oversee the benevolence fund. A deacon serves a three-year term before rotating off for at least one year before they can be nominated again.",
              "marks": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
